// Typecheck-only project: src PLUS test.
//
// tsconfig.json excludes "test", and that exclusion is load-bearing for the
// clean check — `packages/core` ships src and src alone typechecks with zero
// errors, which is a property worth keeping enforceable and fast. But it also
// meant `tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.json` never looked at packages/core/test at
// all: 116 files and 1906 tests, none of them typechecked by anything. `bun
// test` strips types without checking them, so nothing else covered them
// either, and a blatant `const x: number = "nope"` dropped into a test file
// was NOT caught. apps/web has no such hole — its tsconfig includes
// `**/*.ts`, so its 67 test files are checked — which made the gate's coverage
// silently asymmetric between the two workspaces.
//
// This config closes that hole without weakening the one above: the strict
// clean check keeps running over src via tsconfig.json, and this one adds test
// on top, gated by scripts/typecheck-ceiling.mjs because the test tree carries
// a pre-existing backlog (see that file for the count and the argument).
{
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "include": ["src", "test"],
  "exclude": ["node_modules"]
}
